I think a proper solution would be to compare by length, and then if they are the same length, then compare the strings to see if they are really the same. Something like this:

``` c#
public int Compare(string? x, string? y)
{
    // Flip x and y to put the longest instead of the shortest string first in the SortedList.
    var lengthResult = y!.Length.CompareTo(x!.Length);
    if (lengthResult != 0)
    {
        return lengthResult;
    }
    else
    {
        return x!.CompareTo(y);
    }
}
```

